Note: this licence covers the integration this repository adds: the waterbox/
driver, scripts and shims, except where a file says otherwise. Two files say
otherwise because they are made from DuckStation's own source and stay under
its terms (GPL-3.0): waterbox/host.cpp, which began as upstream's
src/duckstation-regtest/regtest_host.cpp, and waterbox/audio-stream.cpp, which
implements the class upstream's src/util/audio_stream.h declares (and, built
for the arcade boards, the one ArcadeDuck's declares). The patches/ directory
modifies DuckStation and the patches-arcade/ directory modifies ArcadeDuck;
each is offered under the terms of what it modifies, which is the GPL-3.0 for
both.

Upstream is DuckStation at commit 14ab642ff3d5d489d388c8062530aa2f7c9a1372
(2024-09-01), the last commit of stenzek/duckstation whose every source file
is offered under the GPL-3.0: the commits after it relicensed the project
under CC BY-NC-ND 4.0, which does not allow a modified version to be
distributed, and nothing from them is here. docs/PLAN.md, "The pin", has the
evidence.

The arcade boards are ArcadeDuck (StillJC/ArcadeDuck), a derivative of that
same DuckStation commit published under the GPL-3.0 only, pinned as its own
submodule and compiled whole beside the console. It bundles processor and
sound-chip emulations under the BSD-3-Clause and MIT licences, several of them
from MAME; its THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.txt lists them.

The built core contains that DuckStation, that ArcadeDuck and the libraries
they bundle, and the package as a whole is therefore distributed under the
GPL-3.0; see waterbox/package-licenses.json.
